Aim
To create a snapshot of an EBS volume, copy it to another AWS region, create a new volume from the snapshot, and attach it to another EC2 instance. 

Procedure
Step 1: Create Snapshot


Go to EC2 Dashboard.


Open:


Volumes




Select EBS volume.


Click:


Actions → Create Snapshot




Enter name and description.


Click Create Snapshot.



Step 2: Copy Snapshot to Another Region


Open:


Snapshots




Select created snapshot.


Click:


Actions → Copy Snapshot




Choose destination AWS region.


Click Copy Snapshot.



Step 3: Monitor Snapshot Status


Wait until snapshot state changes:


Pending → Completed





Step 4: Switch AWS Region


Use region selector at top-right.


Change to destination region.



Step 5: Create Volume from Snapshot


Open:


Snapshots




Select copied snapshot.


Click:


Actions → Create Volume




Configure:


Volume type


Size


Availability Zone




Click Create Volume.



Step 6: Attach Volume to EC2


Go to:


Volumes




Select created volume.


Click:


Actions → Attach Volume




Choose EC2 instance.


Enter device name:
/dev/xvdf


Click Attach.



Step 7: Verify Volume in EC2
SSH into instance and run:
lsblk

Observation


Snapshot created successfully.


Snapshot copied to another AWS region.


New volume created from snapshot.


Volume attached successfully to EC2 instance in destination region. 



Result
Successfully created a snapshot of an EBS volume, copied it to another AWS region, created a new volume from the snapshot, and attached it to another EC2 instance. 
